From 52c65a2cc0bad8d31b061cb2df199a94acb8e502 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Huiwen He <hehuiwen@kylinos.cn>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:05:13 +0800
Subject: [RFC PATCH v2 0/8] ksmbd: improve READ sends and WRITE execution

This series reduces TCP READ payload copies and routes eligible WRITEs to
a CPU-scoped, non-strict unbound workqueue. Worker-owned WRITE responses
can be coalesced without waiting to fill a batch.

The last two patches are separate, default-off experiments: placement
based on observed WRITE overlap, and sending completed WRITE responses
from the receiver. RX now sends individual frames using the existing
work iov; incomplete sends are continued by a TX worker. Startup WRITE
policy requires companion ksmbd-tools support.

A short comparison against the previous RX-coalescing implementation used
1-channel WRITEs, tmpfs, libaio/direct=0/cache=none, on a 128-CPU server
with a local 4-vCPU client. The server used schedutil; client host CPUs
16-23 used performance in both arms. Samples used 15s warmup, 2s ramp and
30s measurement without tracing. READ splice was off; adaptive WRITE
placement and RX sending were on in both arms.

Throughput (MiB/s); changes are medians of paired changes:

 size  jobs  QD  pairs  RX coalescing  RX single-frame  change
   4K    16  32      5         224.89           218.38  +0.82%
   1M     1   2      2        3080.40          3121.06  +1.32%
   1M    16  32      2        3905.42          3942.88  +0.97%

One initial 4 KiB pair dropped 24.69%; three further pairs did not
reproduce it. All samples are retained and its cause is unresolved.
The adaptive on/off comparison on this revision is still pending.

Kernel transport checks covered FIN, paused-reader recovery, interleaved
replies, reset, shutdown and short-send continuation.

Huiwen He (8):
  ksmbd: complete TCP frames before reporting send success
  ksmbd: send READ payloads with MSG_SPLICE_PAGES
  workqueue: export attribute and sysfs setup helpers
  ksmbd: route WRITE requests to an unbound workqueue
  ksmbd: accept WRITE workqueue policy from startup configuration
  ksmbd: coalesce completed WRITE responses
  ksmbd: experiment with per-connection WRITE placement
  ksmbd: experiment with RX-owned WRITE response sending

